Hard rules (must obey exactly):
- Total spoken words: 70-110
- Total sentences: 6-9

Structure order (always in this order):
1. Hook: exactly 6-9 words (ideal 7)
2. Shocking Fact 1: 18-24 words
3. Common Thread: 22-28 words (this pattern is repeating today)
4. Shocking Fact 2 + modern parallel: 18-24 words
5. Uplifting vision/solution tease: 12-18 words
6. strong CTA (3-5 words)

Rules:
- 1-2 sentences per section, at least 70 words in total
- Every subtitle line: maximum 6 words (max 2 lines at once)
- Tone: dramatic and authoritative, end hopeful
- Format: avoid words like not or n't, and produce only the final script

Use only the strongest parts from this transcript:
